course: dictionary
lesson: 15434
title: Statuary: a word for statues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Statuary» means statues, all together as a group. When you meet it, picture a room or garden full of stone or metal figures. «The museum has a large collection of Roman statuary.» The word tells you the museum is showing many statues, not just one.
explain: Statuary is a formal word, so you will meet it in museums, history and art lessons. It is uncountable, so you do not say «a statuary». You say «some statuary» or «the statuary». «The garden of the grand house was filled with garden statuary: stone lions, marble gods and angels.» The list of things tells you what kind of statues are meant.
explain: The word can also mean the art of making statues. «The students spent the afternoon learning statuary in the art room.» The clue is the word learning: you learn a skill, not a pile of statues. Ask yourself: are the words about things, or about a skill? That tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Statuary means statues together, as a group.
fact: «Statuary» is a formal, rather stiff word, found in museums, history books and art lessons.
fact: Statuary is uncountable: say «some statuary» or «the statuary», not «a statuary».
fact: «Roman statuary» means Roman statues together.
fact: «Garden statuary» means statues in a garden.
fact: Statuary can also mean the art of making statues.
exercise: «The museum has a fine collection of Roman statuary.» What does statuary mean here? | Coins and old pots | Paintings on the walls | *Statues together as a group | A type of stone floor
exercise: «She went to art school to learn statuary.» What does statuary mean here? | Paper and paint | A group of statues in a garden | *The art of making statues | A large, dark cave
exercise: Which sentence uses statuary correctly? | *«The museum has some statuary.» | «The museum has a statuary.» | «The museum has three statuaries.» | «The museum has many statuaries.»
test: What does statuary mean? | *Statues together, as a group | A kind of bird | A very long train journey | Old coins from long ago
test: «The guide showed us the statuary in the hall, and the marble heroes looked down at us.» What does statuary mean here? | Shouting and noise | *Statues in the hall | Heroes who are alive | A type of hall lighting
exam: In «The students spent the afternoon learning statuary in the art room», what does statuary mean? | A lunch of soup and bread | *The art of making statues | Painting landscapes | Singing in a choir
